//! Batch publishing subscribers: consume a batch, publish the derived replies, then ack.
//!
//! Generated by `#[subscriber("in", reply("reply-name"))]` on a `&[T]` handler and mounted with
//! [`BrokerScope::include`](https://docs.rs/ruststream/latest/ruststream/runtime/struct.BrokerScope.html#method.include), chaining
//! [`.out(Reply, ..)`](super::RouterWith::out) to name the reply publish policy (without it, the
//! statement commits with the broker's default policy); on a [`Router`](super::Router) the same
//! chain ends in `.build()`, which is what commits the
//! registration. At startup the wiring pairs into a [`ReplyPublisher`]: a plain one publishes
//! each reply independently, while a `.transactional()` one makes the whole batch's replies
//! visible atomically - the consume-transform-produce pattern.

